        "original_id": "a83556fe-7737-5390-84ec-a25b7620b817",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Kanin, Ring Lardner Jr., Katharine Hepburn, Spencer Tracy\n- Works: Woman of the Year, When I Grow Up\n- Awards: Academy Award\n- Topics: Hollywood blacklist, Red Scare\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Kanin was born on February 1, 1910, and he was an American director, producer, playwright, and screenwriter.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was born on August 19, 1915, and he was an American journalist and screenwriter.\n- In 1942, Michael Kanin shared an Academy Award with Ring Lardner Jr. for writing the Katharine Hepburn-Spencer Tracy film comedy \"Woman of the Year.\"\n- During the late 1940s and 1950s, Ring Lardner Jr. was blacklisted by Hollywood movie studios during the Red Scare.\n- In 1951, Michael Kanin wrote and directed the American drama film \"When I Grow Up.\"\n- Michael Kanin died on March 12, 1993.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. died on October 31, 2000.",
